<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/target/procedural-constraint> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/lossyDrop> "a hand-authored CLOSED-WORLD lint whose finding is SUPERSEDED by RDFS/OWL entailment is not projected as a logic:Constraint: e.g. gmeow:CoreObservationMethodShape flags a gmeow:TemporalMeasurement carrying only gmeow:measurementMethod for a missing gmeow:observationMethod, but gmeow:measurementMethod rdfs:subPropertyOf gmeow:observationMethod entails the method, so the canonical logic: reasoning layer proves the datum well-formed — a faithful closed-world projection cannot reproduce that finding without contradicting the entailment (it would over-claim), so the finding is a reasoning artifact carried in the canonical logic: layer and its hand-authored shape is retained as a closed-world lint (dating1 residue)" .
