<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/target/shacl-af> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/lossyDrop> "actual: ground axiom <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleFrontierBlockedPrecondition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"frontier label: blocked on an unmet precondition\" is an asserted fact (not a class/property subsumption), so it has no SHACL-AF sh:SPARQLRule derivation form and is carried in the canonical RDF-1.2 layer" .
<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/target/shacl-af> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/lossyDrop> "actual: ground axiom <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleFrontierBlockedPrecondition> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Derives logic:FrontierBlockedPrecondition for a frontier entry whose step axis is pending — the step belongs to the enactment and its preconditions have not been evaluated as met, which is exactly the position the step axis mints for an unmet precondition. Positive Horn, and disjoint from every other rule by the step axis alone. The label matters because its remedy differs from every neighbouring obstruction: a precondition is remediable by changing the world, where a missing capability is not, and telling an operator to wait when the answer is to change the world is the failure this separation prevents.\" is an asserted fact (not a class/property subsumption), so it has no SHACL-AF sh:SPARQLRule derivation form and is carried in the canonical RDF-1.2 layer" .
