<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/target/shacl-af> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/lossyDrop> "actual: ground axiom <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleFrontierCancelled> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"frontier label: cancelled\" is an asserted fact (not a class/property subsumption), so it has no SHACL-AF sh:SPARQLRule derivation form and is carried in the canonical RDF-1.2 layer" .
<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/target/shacl-af> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/lossyDrop> "actual: ground axiom <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleFrontierCancelled> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Derives logic:FrontierCancelled for a frontier entry whose step and enactment axes are both cancelled and whose commitment knowledge was never evaluated — the quiescent cancellation, where stopping by decision settles the matter because no external effect was ever in question. The knowledge position is the load-bearing conjunct: it is what distinguishes this from cancellation with in-flight effects, and reading a bare cancelled position as quiescent is exactly how an outstanding exchange gets closed on paper while remaining open at the provider.\" is an asserted fact (not a class/property subsumption), so it has no SHACL-AF sh:SPARQLRule derivation form and is carried in the canonical RDF-1.2 layer" .
