<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/target/shacl-af> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/lossyDrop> "actual: ground axiom <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleFrontierCancelledWithInFlightEffects> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"frontier label: cancelled with in-flight effects\" is an asserted fact (not a class/property subsumption), so it has no SHACL-AF sh:SPARQLRule derivation form and is carried in the canonical RDF-1.2 layer" .
<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/target/shacl-af> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/lossyDrop> "actual: ground axiom <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleFrontierCancelledWithInFlightEffects> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Derives logic:FrontierCancelledWithInFlightEffects for a frontier entry whose step and enactment axes are both cancelled while its commitment knowledge remains undetermined. Cancellation is a decision about the occurrence and it does not resolve knowledge about the world, so the outstanding exchange still demands reconciliation; the sibling entry that positions that exchange reads reconciliation-required. It differs from plain cancelled on the commitment-knowledge axis and on nothing else, which is exactly why the two cannot share a slot — and it is arguably the hardest real position an operator meets, which a bare cancelled label hides.\" is an asserted fact (not a class/property subsumption), so it has no SHACL-AF sh:SPARQLRule derivation form and is carried in the canonical RDF-1.2 layer" .
