<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/target/shacl-af> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/lossyDrop> "actual: ground axiom <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleFrontierCompensationEligible> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Derives logic:FrontierCompensationEligible for a frontier entry whose effect axis sits at receipted — a forward effect is known to have committed, so a counteraction is now permissible. Eligibility is all this derives: it asserts no compensation attempt, no compensation outcome, and no claim that compensating will succeed, because compensation is a new action with its own possibility of failing.\" is an asserted fact (not a class/property subsumption), so it has no SHACL-AF sh:SPARQLRule derivation form and is carried in the canonical RDF-1.2 layer" .
