<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/target/shacl-af> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/lossyDrop> "actual: ground axiom <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleFrontierCompensationFailedForwardCommitted> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"frontier label: compensation failed with the forward effect committed\" is an asserted fact (not a class/property subsumption), so it has no SHACL-AF sh:SPARQLRule derivation form and is carried in the canonical RDF-1.2 layer" .
<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/target/shacl-af> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/lossyDrop> "actual: ground axiom <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleFrontierCompensationFailedForwardCommitted> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Derives logic:FrontierCompensationFailedForwardCommitted for a frontier entry whose exchange sits in its compensating leg, whose step axis is failed, whose commitment knowledge is still supported, and whose enactment is still running. Read together those four positions say the whole thing: a compensating action was launched, the step carrying it terminally failed, the forward effect it was launched against remains committed, and the occurrence has not given up. The last position is what separates this from terminally-failed — the enactment is still running because escalation is a continuation, and escalation rather than retry is the only move this position licenses.\" is an asserted fact (not a class/property subsumption), so it has no SHACL-AF sh:SPARQLRule derivation form and is carried in the canonical RDF-1.2 layer" .
