<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/target/shacl-af> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/lossyDrop> "actual: ground axiom <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleFrontierCompensationRequired> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Derives logic:FrontierCompensationRequired for a frontier entry whose effect axis sits at reconciled, whose commitment knowledge is supported, and whose enactment axis is failed — a probe settled that the forward effect committed, and the occurrence it belonged to will not complete, so the committed effect has to be counteracted for the run to reach a consistent terminal position. Three axes carry this and none of them could alone: the effect position says the question was answered, the knowledge value says which way, and the enactment position is what turns permission into obligation. That is precisely what separates it from compensation-eligible, where declining costs nothing.\" is an asserted fact (not a class/property subsumption), so it has no SHACL-AF sh:SPARQLRule derivation form and is carried in the canonical RDF-1.2 layer" .
