<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/target/shacl-af> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/lossyDrop> "actual: ground axiom <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleFrontierCompleted> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Derives logic:FrontierCompleted for a frontier entry whose step axis is completed — the step carried out its prescribed work and reached a terminal position, so nothing further is owed on it. The guard reads that one axis and stops there on purpose: the label asserts nothing about whether the enactment's goal is met, which is the goal-evaluation axis, and nothing about whether an external effect the step dispatched actually committed, which is the commitment-knowledge axis carried by the exchange's own entry.\" is an asserted fact (not a class/property subsumption), so it has no SHACL-AF sh:SPARQLRule derivation form and is carried in the canonical RDF-1.2 layer" .
