<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/target/shacl-af> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/lossyDrop> "actual: ground axiom <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleFrontierMutuallyExclusive> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"frontier label: mutually exclusive with another candidate\" is an asserted fact (not a class/property subsumption), so it has no SHACL-AF sh:SPARQLRule derivation form and is carried in the canonical RDF-1.2 layer" .
<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/target/shacl-af> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/lossyDrop> "actual: ground axiom <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleFrontierMutuallyExclusive> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Derives logic:FrontierMutuallyExclusive for a frontier entry that logic:entryExcludes another entry. This is the one guard in the set that reads no axis, and deliberately: exclusivity is a relation between two candidates and not a position either of them occupies, so putting it on an axis would be the conflation the seven-axis discipline exists to refuse. It becomes visible only when local frontiers are glued, which is also why the withheld candidate carries no readiness position — being ready is a claim about a frontier on which the excluding candidate was not taken.\" is an asserted fact (not a class/property subsumption), so it has no SHACL-AF sh:SPARQLRule derivation form and is carried in the canonical RDF-1.2 layer" .
