<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/target/shacl-af> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/lossyDrop> "actual: ground axiom <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleFrontierReadyApprovalRequired> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"frontier label: ready but approval required\" is an asserted fact (not a class/property subsumption), so it has no SHACL-AF sh:SPARQLRule derivation form and is carried in the canonical RDF-1.2 layer" .
<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/target/shacl-af> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/lossyDrop> "actual: ground axiom <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleFrontierReadyApprovalRequired> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Derives logic:FrontierReadyApprovalRequired for a frontier entry whose step axis is ready and whose approval axis is created but not yet detached. Readiness and approval are separate axes, and this rule is where that separation earns its keep: the same entry is simultaneously ready to run and gated, which a single blended state could only express by minting a combined value for every such pairing.\" is an asserted fact (not a class/property subsumption), so it has no SHACL-AF sh:SPARQLRule derivation form and is carried in the canonical RDF-1.2 layer" .
