<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/target/shacl-af> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/lossyDrop> "actual: ground axiom <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleFrontierReadyAuthorized> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Derives logic:FrontierReadyAuthorized for a frontier entry whose step axis is ready and whose approval axis is null — the policy already authorizes the effect, so no operator gate stands between the action and its dispatch. Positive Horn. This is the rule that makes policy-maximal automation a derivation rather than a habit: an entry is authorized because its axis tuple says so, not because nobody remembered to gate it.\" is an asserted fact (not a class/property subsumption), so it has no SHACL-AF sh:SPARQLRule derivation form and is carried in the canonical RDF-1.2 layer" .
