<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/target/shacl-af> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/lossyDrop> "actual: ground axiom <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleFrontierReconciliationImpossible> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Derives logic:FrontierReconciliationImpossible for a frontier entry whose effect axis sits at abandoned — the exchange was given up without an authoritative determination because no reconciliation semantics remain available. The effect axis mints exactly one position for that, so the guard needs nothing else. The label is the honest counterpart of reconciliation-required: there, probing is still available and the frontier names it; here it is foreclosed, and naming another probe would send an operator after evidence that cannot be obtained.\" is an asserted fact (not a class/property subsumption), so it has no SHACL-AF sh:SPARQLRule derivation form and is carried in the canonical RDF-1.2 layer" .
<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/target/shacl-af> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/lossyDrop> "actual: ground axiom <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleFrontierReconciliationImpossible> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/body> <c14n42> is an asserted fact (not a class/property subsumption), so it has no SHACL-AF sh:SPARQLRule derivation form and is carried in the canonical RDF-1.2 layer" .
