<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/target/shacl-af> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/lossyDrop> "actual: ground axiom <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleFrontierReconciliationRequired> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"frontier label: reconciliation required\" is an asserted fact (not a class/property subsumption), so it has no SHACL-AF sh:SPARQLRule derivation form and is carried in the canonical RDF-1.2 layer" .
<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/target/shacl-af> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/lossyDrop> "actual: ground axiom <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleFrontierReconciliationRequired> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Derives logic:FrontierReconciliationRequired for a frontier entry whose effect axis sits at attempted — an effect was dispatched and no receipt settled it. This is the no-blind-retry law stated positively: rather than only forbidding a retry, the frontier NAMES the one action that is licensed from an undetermined position, so an operator reading it is told what to do instead of merely what not to do.\" is an asserted fact (not a class/property subsumption), so it has no SHACL-AF sh:SPARQLRule derivation form and is carried in the canonical RDF-1.2 layer" .
