<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/target/shacl-af> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/lossyDrop> "actual: ground axiom <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleFrontierSkippedWithTypedReason> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"frontier label: skipped with a typed reason\" is an asserted fact (not a class/property subsumption), so it has no SHACL-AF sh:SPARQLRule derivation form and is carried in the canonical RDF-1.2 layer" .
<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/target/shacl-af> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/lossyDrop> "actual: ground axiom <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleFrontierSkippedWithTypedReason> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Derives logic:FrontierSkippedWithTypedReason for a frontier entry whose step axis is skipped and which carries a logic:skipReason. The typed reason is a guard and not a decoration: the label's whole content is that the omission was deliberate and attributable, so an entry claiming a skip without one derives nothing rather than deriving a label it cannot support — which is the correct outcome, because an untyped skip is indistinguishable from an oversight and the frontier must not present the two alike.\" is an asserted fact (not a class/property subsumption), so it has no SHACL-AF sh:SPARQLRule derivation form and is carried in the canonical RDF-1.2 layer" .
<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/target/shacl-af> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/lossyDrop> "actual: ground axiom <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleFrontierSkippedWithTypedReason> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/body> <c14n29> is an asserted fact (not a class/property subsumption), so it has no SHACL-AF sh:SPARQLRule derivation form and is carried in the canonical RDF-1.2 layer" .
