<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/target/shacl-af> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/lossyDrop> "actual: ground axiom <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleFrontierTerminallyFailed> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"frontier label: terminally failed\" is an asserted fact (not a class/property subsumption), so it has no SHACL-AF sh:SPARQLRule derivation form and is carried in the canonical RDF-1.2 layer" .
<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/target/shacl-af> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/lossyDrop> "actual: ground axiom <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleFrontierTerminallyFailed> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Derives logic:FrontierTerminallyFailed for a frontier entry whose step axis is failed and whose enactment axis is failed — the step attempted its work and failed, and the occurrence stopped because no continuation is available, which is the enactment axis's own definition of failure. Both conjuncts are needed: a failed step inside a still-running enactment has a continuation somewhere, and the enactment position is what says there is none. That is also what separates it from compensation-failed-forward-committed, where the run is still going because escalation remains open.\" is an asserted fact (not a class/property subsumption), so it has no SHACL-AF sh:SPARQLRule derivation form and is carried in the canonical RDF-1.2 layer" .
