<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/target/shacl-af> <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/lossyDrop> "actual: ground axiom <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleFrontierWaitingOnEventTimeOrInput> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Derives logic:FrontierWaitingOnEventTimeOrInput for a frontier entry whose step axis is waiting and which names, through logic:entryAwaits, the thing it is blocked pending. The awaited witness is what makes the label a derivation rather than a shrug: the step axis says THAT the step waits, and only the witness says what would end the wait. It is also what keeps this rule disjoint from the capability-gap rule, which shares the waiting position — a step blocked by a capability the deployment does not have awaits nothing, because what is absent does not arrive, and its remedy is a capability-gap proposal rather than patience.\" is an asserted fact (not a class/property subsumption), so it has no SHACL-AF sh:SPARQLRule derivation form and is carried in the canonical RDF-1.2 layer" .
